{"record": "turn", "turn": 4, "seconds": 6.63, "response_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "stop_reason": "tool_use", "stop_details": null, "blocks": ["thinking", "tool_use"], "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 2322}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 2322, "cache_read_input_tokens": 8945, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 1076, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "speed": "standard"}, "tools": [{"id": "toolu_0127qhdX23AJgr3X7rsmdKNg", "name": "submit_answer", "arguments": {"answer": "No. The two analyses use different likelihood-ratio thresholds and profile different nuisance parameters.\n\n- dSph gamma-ray limits: the one-sided upper limit is set where 2[ln L_max − ln L(⟨σv⟩₉₅)] = 2.71, a drop of 2.71 in TS (1.355 in ln L). The profiled nuisance parameter is each dwarf's J-factor normalization (J = s·J₀). A Gaussian prior in log₁₀s is profiled over [−3, 3], with width set by the quoted uncertainty in log₁₀J.\n- AMS-02 antiproton limits: the limit is the upper endpoint of the ΔQ ≤ 3.84 region, where Q = −2 ln L. The paper calls this the nominal 95% threshold for one parameter of interest. It says this differs from the usual one-sided 95% prescription (2.71). The profiled nuisance parameter is the Galactic diffusive-halo half-height L. It has a Gaussian penalty in log₁₀L (L̂ = 4.96 kpc, σ = 0.197) and is profiled over 1–12 kpc.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.2"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "5"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.3"}]}, "status": "answer", "error_kind": null, "seconds": 0.0}]}
{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261123T034356Z_dev-02_staged_8477", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "No. The two analyses use different likelihood-ratio thresholds and profile different nuisance parameters.\n\n- dSph gamma-ray limits: the one-sided upper limit is set where 2[ln L_max − ln L(⟨σv⟩₉₅)] = 2.71, a drop of 2.71 in TS (1.355 in ln L). The profiled nuisance parameter is each dwarf's J-factor normalization (J = s·J₀). A Gaussian prior in log₁₀s is profiled over [−3, 3], with width set by the quoted uncertainty in log₁₀J.\n- AMS-02 antiproton limits: the limit is the upper endpoint of the ΔQ ≤ 3.84 region, where Q = −2 ln L. The paper calls this the nominal 95% threshold for one parameter of interest. It says this differs from the usual one-sided 95% prescription (2.71). The profiled nuisance parameter is the Galactic diffusive-halo half-height L. It has a Gaussian penalty in log₁₀L (L̂ = 4.96 kpc, σ = 0.197) and is profiled over 1–12 kpc.", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.2"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "5"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "4.3"}]}, "asked_again": null, "turns": 4, "seconds": 12.185, "tool_calls": 4, "tool_result_chars": 19594, "input_tokens": 10, "output_tokens": 1395, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 11267, "cache_read_input_tokens": 15360, "parser_versions": ["4"], "response_models": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "ended_at": "2026-11-23T03:44:08+00:00"}
